# Canonical policy

This repo is strict-next-ranger, a strict Next.js 16 frontend operating system. The
documentation corpus is the source of truth — consult it before changing structure:

- `AGENTS.md` — universal agent entrypoint and skills routing table
- `context/architecture-map.md` — where everything lives
- `rules/00-non-negotiable-rules.md` — the full law; `rules/` holds per-topic rules 01–20
- `skills/` — step-by-step procedures for every recurring task
- `memory/known-pitfalls.md` — mistakes already made once; do not repeat them
- `docs/eslint/` — one page per custom `frontend-architecture` rule

# Non-negotiables

- Third-party packages are imported ONLY through their owning wrapper in
  `src/packages/<vendor>` (ownership map: `eslint/package-boundaries.config.mjs`).
- Cross-module imports ONLY via the module public surface `@/modules/<feature>`.
- `*.component.tsx` files are TSX-only: no hooks, no logic, no inline declarations,
  no raw copy, no raw `className` outside the design system.
- Containers carry `'use client'` + a `// client-boundary-reason: …` comment.
- No `process.env` outside `src/packages/env`; no browser globals outside
  `src/packages/browser` / `src/packages/storage`.
- Query keys only from `*-query-keys.ts` builders; `useAppQuery`/`useAppMutation` only.
- Every user-visible string is a next-intl message key with `en` and `ar` entries.
- Never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Never `eslint-disable` without a documented
  exception in `docs/exceptions/` — move the code to the right layer instead.
- TDD; coverage 95% global, 100% for utils/helpers/mappers/schemas/query-key builders.
- Before finishing any task run: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test`,
  `npm run build` (or the aggregate `npm run quality`).
